<title>SWEDEN: NCC says Ericsson to rent German complex.</title>
<headline>NCC says Ericsson to rent German complex.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish construction group NCC said on Wednesday telecoms group LM Ericsson AB's would rent 80 percent of its planned 450 million crown Neues Zentrum Seestern complex in the German city of Dusseldorf, with an option to rent the remainder.  </p>
<p>&quot;The total investment amounts to around 450 million crowns. Building recently began and the project will be completed by September 30, 1998,&quot; NCC said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom, +46-8-700 1006</p>
</text>
